# TODO - Reuse the maximum useful upstream driver implementation

## Owner directive — 2026-11-10

Review all three repositories below in depth. Copy or adapt as much useful,
license-compatible implementation as possible to finish SimpleATH's required
production paths faster. Prefer proven reusable implementations to rewriting
working code. Integrate imported code with real AR9565 callers in the normal
target; collecting unused files or adding attribution alone is not completion.
This supports **FIRST IMPLEMENTATION, THEN CORRECTION** and does not reduce
the Wi-Fi, Bluetooth/BLE, AWDL/AirDrop, power or recovery objective.

The latest owner instruction leaves independently authored SimpleATH code
without a repository-wide license grant, as a public personal/research project.
Preserve every upstream copyright, license, modification notice and source
obligation. GPL-2.0 components and their derivatives retain their GPL terms;
public/personal use does not override them or NullMoth's noncommercial terms.
Assess distribution of combined derivatives under the applicable upstream
licenses; do not assume that removing the project license permits mixing.
The GPLv2 text is retained separately under licenses/GPL-2.0.txt.

## Pinned review sources and concrete reuse candidates

1. [AirPort_RTW89](https://github.com/FranciumOS-org/AirPort_RTW89/tree/90b6cfc5a69c271688fad188857cfaeb58053dc5),
   revision `90b6cfc5a69c271688fad188857cfaeb58053dc5`.
   Review `src/front/AirPortRTW89Front.*`, `src/front/rtw89_front_api.h`,
   `src/kext/AirPortRTW89Native.cpp` and the relevant `src/compat_rtw89/`
   scan, association, WPA2, framing and AWDL code. Its own source declares
   GPL-2.0; vendored components have per-file licenses. Adapt native request
   handling, callback lifetime, PMK/handshake ownership, scan completion and
   packet delivery where compatible with the exact target. This frontend
   uses restored IO80211FamilyLegacy, not our modern 25G332 InfraProtocol ABI.
   Its README explicitly leaves AirDrop/AWDL/Continuity unfinished.
2. [AirportItlwm-BE200](https://github.com/Ersiter/AirportItlwm-BE200/tree/ff82f3e5647ce3885f5d48417b6356a6a23d2163),
   revision `ff82f3e5647ce3885f5d48417b6356a6a23d2163`.
   Review `AirportItlwm/WCL/WCL.*`, `AirportItlwmSkywalkInterface.*`,
   `AirportItlwmV2.*`, `AirportItlwmEthernetInterface.*` and relevant
   OpenBSD-derived net80211 source. Root licensing is GPL-2.0; preserve each
   file's own terms. Reuse the modern WCL scan/BSS, join/PMK, event, private
   MAC and lifetime implementations after checking exact 25G332 contracts.
   Do not copy its fake `getProvider()` Ethernet bridge or advertise Intel
   firmware/HE/EHT/MLO/6 GHz behavior as AR9565 hardware support. README and
   branch development notes make different claims; inspect actual source.
3. [NullMoth NVIDIA driver](https://github.com/nullmoth/nvidia-macos-driver/tree/7412cdde81447f78da0ebb64216dc258d8beaedb),
   revision `7412cdde81447f78da0ebb64216dc258d8beaedb`.
   Review `docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md`, `docs/SLEEP-WAKE.md`, `LICENSE` and `NOTICE`
   for IOKit ownership, suspend/resume sequencing and actionable diagnostics.
   The project's own `kexts/`, `plugin/`, `build/` and `package/` code is
   **PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0**, not GPL-compatible merely because it
   uses GPL/MIT dependencies. Its restriction to permitted noncommercial
   purposes cannot be added to a GPL-2.0 combined work (GPLv2 section 6).
   Assess independently licensed MIT/BSD upstream components separately when
   relevant; do not copy unrelated graphics code. Otherwise use architectural
   facts and public IOKit APIs for an independently authored implementation.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Inventory applicable source files and licenses at the pinned revisions.
      Record concrete destination scopes, changes and retained notices for
      imports, and precise reasons for portions that cannot apply.
- [ ] Adapt all useful compatible implementations that close required native
      control, scan/join/WPA2, data, power/recovery or AWDL/BLE integration gaps.
      Do not stop after reading READMEs or drafting a reuse plan.
- [ ] Connect every adapted implementation to real production callers and the
      Xcode target; remove displaced duplicate or passive paths.
- [ ] Preserve original authorship and full required notices in copied files
      and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Keep firmware licensing separate.
- [ ] Check byte layouts, ownership, gate order and real error propagation
      against the exact target and AR9565 contracts; no copied success stubs,
      invented capabilities or permanently disabled required functionality.
- [ ] Run meaningful offline regressions for imported behavior and record
      their actual scope. Whole-project zero-failure validation follows full
      implementation; mandatory CI remains before every kernel build.

## Initial evidence — not completion

Pinned source/license trees and relevant native frontend/WCL files were read
through the native terminal on 2026-11-10. The reference comparison confirms
that macOS can supply a PMK while the driver must still own the four-way
handshake; the existing native OS-supplicant assumption is not sufficient for
the modern WCL join. Resolve this in the real owner/crypto contract, with one
handshake owner, before claiming WPA2 completion. Modern packet factory and
queue contracts remain independently checked against the exact KDK.
No new kext build, installation, EFI change or hardware test is authorized
by this TODO. Source completeness and physical verification remain separate.
